НD„Н3|сЙНг{Press any key to continue:␀Н3„НХ{Г3|НпНг{------------------------------------------␀Нг{|  Hard Disk Backup/Restoration Utility  |␀Нг{|                                        |␀Нг{|  Beta Test Version B        20 Nov 87  |␀Нг{|                                        |␀Нг{|           by Steve Dirickson           |␀Нг{	------------------------------------------␀НпНг{-------------------------------------------------------------------------␀Нг{|BUSH, the BackUp SHell, is an integrated hard disk backup & restoration|␀Нг{|utility for use under ZCPR3.  It provides a convenient, single-program |␀Нг{|manager for the control of full or partial backups of hard disk files  |␀Нг{|to floppy disks, and for full or selective restoration of the archived |␀Нг{|files.  A variety of file selection options are available, both during |␀Нг{|the backup and when restoring files.  A backup operation may be inter- |␀Нг{|rupted at any time and resumed later from the same point, with the same|␀Нг{|file selections still in effect.  Miscellaneous options such as printer|␀Нг{|logging and read-after-write verification are also available.          |␀Нг{|Extensive in-context help is available at all levels of operation.     |␀Нг{|                                                                       |␀Нг{|    [Press any key for next screen]                                    |␀Нг{-------------------------------------------------------------------------␀Н3„Нг{BUSH relies heavily on the facilities of the Z System.  As a minimum,  ␀Нг{the following Z System modules must be present in your installation:   ␀Нг{                                                                       ␀Нг{       Command Line Buffer                                             ␀Нг{       Shell Stack                                                     ␀Нг{       External File Control Block (EXTFCB)                            ␀Нг{       Environment Descriptor, including TCAP segment                  ␀Нг{                                                                       ␀Нг{Since these are standard components in most ZCPR3 implementations,     ␀Нг{BUSH should run on your system with no requirement for modifications.  ␀Н3„Нг{Note that, due to the amount of code required to provide the advanced  ␀Нг{capabilities of BUSH, the program is made up of a main driver program, ␀Нг{BUSH.COM, and a series of 'subroutines', called 'BUSH!x.COM', where 'x'␀Нг{is a number or letter.  These files must all be located either in a    ␀Нг{specified DU (which may be selected by patching the BUSH.COM file--see ␀Нг{the section on Configuration), or they may be located anywhere along   ␀Нг{the current path, and BUSH will find them there.  BUSH will load the   ␀Нг{'subroutine' files as it needs them, as long as they can be found in   ␀Нг{one of the two locations listed.  These subroutine programs pass       ␀Нг{control back to BUSH via the shell stack.                              ␀Нг{    [Press any key to start]          ␀Н3„НХ{Н‚|!ѕvН–sНХ{НgНпН‚|!ћsНХ{~·ИНQѓш  @@@@@@@@@@@@        @@          @@        @@@@@@@@@@        @@           @@
