First (and only) in 70-79 division in New Milford Moonlight 5k. 28:43. Out
and back fairly flat.

MCT - Saturday, June 3, 2017 at 14:28:43 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Ran the Go Fast Go Far 5Kish in Durham this morning. Finish time was 26:31.
I say 5kish because it was 3.09 and apparently the RD agrees it was not a
true 5K. Fun race around the Durham Fair grounds. Also did 5 miles earlier
this morning at home.

<a href=https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1775486356>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1775486356</a>

lrb - Saturday, June 3, 2017 at 21:57:05 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Ran 2 5ks today, 9 AM in Chaplin, 1 PM in Harwinton. towns 103 and 104.

Chaplin: 29:54 9:41 pace 1st in division - lollypop course, hilly

<a href=https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1776316095>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1776316095</a>

Harwinton: 33:28 10:42 out and back, flat. MUCH slower than 1st race. BBQ
after. 2nd in division.

<a href=https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1776316084>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1776316084</a>

MCT - Sunday, June 4, 2017 at 16:41:54 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Ran the Goodwin Forest 10K today. 1:09 and just under 10K at 5.7 miles. Saw
Joe there before the race but he was out on the 30K course. I also did 5
miles early this morning. 58 miles for the week.

<a href=https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1777976892>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1777976892</a>

ceb - Tuesday, June 6, 2017 at 01:41:41 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Been feeling a little under the weather in the last 4 days.  It seems
to be some intestinal flu thing.  Don't have much of an appetite. I
ran 3 tonight for the first time since last Monday.  Having oatmeal
for dinner.  Exciting!  Didn't achive my 18 mile plan last week.  Did
6 instead.

<IMG SRC = NRRC.JPG>

Finished hanging 23 pieces of art work in the NH gallery
today.  Looks good.  Came home and took a long nap.  If the flu thing
doesn't improve in the next day or two I may get it checked out.

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1780820329>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1780820329</a>

lrb - Thursday, June 8, 2017 at 19:18:07 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

<a href=http://plattsys.com/m1shell.php?eventid=1597>http://plattsys.com/m1shell.php?eventid=1597</a>

Ran Solstice Sprint 5k last nite. 2nd in 70s. Bob Ward way ahead. I took
29 minutes.

<a href=https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1785713674>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1785713674</a>

Linda took pix. Posted some on Facebook.

<a href=https://www.facebook.com/media/set/?set=oa.1963104127253808&type=1>https://www.facebook.com/media/set/?set=oa.1963104127253808&type=1</a>

Linda and I are heading to Portsmouth, NH on Friday for Saturday 10k. Brent
is running it too.

MCT - Friday, June 9, 2017 at 11:12:47 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Did a loop around the Lake Garda school. 7 miles and with the big hill. This
is day #850 in the streak. This week we officially put our home up for sale
and have a deposit in Canton on a condo. I will live right on the Rails to
Trails. I can run, walk, ride a bike anytime(once I'm retired). If you ever
ran the Lobster Loop 5K in Canton I and 1/10th of a mile from the start line.
Therefore I'm moving but still a Connecticut  runner. I'm running the Nipmuck
South Trail race this Sunday.

<a href=https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1786623161>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1786623161</a>

tlz - Sunday, June 11, 2017 at 01:49:56 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

I ran twice on the ship - 4.5 miles and 5 miles.  2.91 times around the deck
was equal to 1 mile. The second time I ran was on our way back to NJ.  The
wind was blowing like crazy and it was raining pretty hard at times.  There
were a couple of other brave souls out there so I decided to run as well.
Shared a couple of laps with an 11th grade girl who does cross-country.
So for this week so far I ran:

Wed. - 5 miles on the ship
Thurs. - 6 miles back home
Fri. - 6 miles
Sat. - 6 miles

All were between 9:45 and 10:00 min. pace.  Thankfully, my ankle is feeling
better.

Nice job, Lee and Brent, on the 10K!

Mike, good luck on your trail race tomorrow! 

