ceb - Friday, June 30, 2017 at 19:20:39 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Yesterday I went to Barre, MA to walk on a path that is
used by meditators there at the <a href = https://www.google.com/search?q=barre+meditation&ie=utf-8&oe=utf-8#q=barre+meditation&rflfq=1&rlha=0&rllag=42449310,-72121632,305&tbm=lcl&tbs=lrf:!2m1!1e2!2m1!1e3!3sEAE,lf:1,lf_ui:2&rlfi=hd:;si:427773285721535737;mv:!1m3!1d1993.3239143344838!2d-72.12163204999999!3d42.449310249999996!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i145!2i130!4f13.1;tbs:lrf:!2m1!1e2!2m1!1e3!3sEAE,lf:1,lf_ui:2>Barre Insight Meditation Society</a>
I walked (not meditating) 4.4 miles on a very peaceful, forest-lined country road with
surounding farms, wildlife, and old homes some of which looked as if
they had been there forever.  Old rusted farm equipment, a barking
dog and a tiny chipmunk on the top center of a huge boulder were among
the many sights.  I missed a turn (I was following a map) onto
Lover's Lane (appropriately named) which made the walk a little
longer than 3 miles.  Here is the map of the <a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1826259701>walk</a>
The walking pace was 21:53 / mile.

Ran 7.0 miles today in 1:04:23, 9:12/mile pace.

<img src=FH.JPG> 

Really felt the heat and humidity today.  Took the 
Groton route via James Brook Road. Some hills. Full sun and sweat!
 
<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1827557409>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1827557409</a>

