<body>

<table align=center width=89%><tr><td>

<pre><a href=http://primepuzzle.com/runlog/may_2017.htm><img title="Brickyarders' Log" src=http://primepuzzle.com/tpf/bricks.61.25.jpg></a><font size=+1><b>

MCT - Monday, May 1, 2017 at 10:26:06 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Had a great time at Lake Waramaug. Shitty time of approx 6:38. My Garmin battery
ran out at mile 29 and I couldn't find the time keeper for my finish time.
Nice to see everyone though. Today I did a slow 5 miles with a 13:23 pace.

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1708156422>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1708156422</a>

tlz - Monday, May 1, 2017 at 10:40:27 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

OMG Mike, you ran 5 miles today!  Joe and I are walking around like crippled
old folks.  LOL  I wouldn't even be able to run a mile today.  

I asked for my time right after the race and the time keeper said 5:22. 
I was so annoyed and told him that was 20+ min. off - in the wrong direction!
He claimed that once he got the data from the timing mats, etc., my correct
time would be reflected.  I've never had that happen in the previous 6 years.
In fact, they usually  print out the results and have them on a board to
view.  Mike Melton, who is always there to do the timing, sent someone else
this year. I made sure to tell Rob, one of the race directors, that it wasn't
correct and I emailed Rob and Mike Melton at MCM timing yesterday with my
Garmin data.  I also didn't like that Rob started the race 3 min. early with
no warning.  I tried to make the best of it and thought maybe it helped me
to run the out and back a little faster than I normally would have.  But
I had no idea who was ahead of me.  Didn't matter I suppose as the 3 or 4
women ahead of me blew me away with their times.

Anyway, your endurance and recovery is super impressive.  I could use some
of that for the 48 hour!

lrb - Monday, May 1, 2017 at 11:25:01 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

<a href=https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1708290416>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1708290416</a>

This was my one looper w/ Mike yesterday. Tray, the timer was Mike Melton's
son. I'm sure they'll fix the error based on your Garmin. Super well done,
both of you.

tlz - Tuesday, May 2, 2017 at 00:37:36 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Results are up and my time is correct - 4th out of 31 females and 15th out
of 65 total 50K runners. :)

<a href=http://mcmtiming.com/>http://mcmtiming.com/</a> 

MCT - Tuesday, May 2, 2017 at 10:47:55 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Congratulations Tracy. Outstanding considering you hadn't trained much. I
did 8 miles this morning in Hyannis MA at a 11:57 pace. Tough at the start
but loosened up as I went along. BTW...yesterday I didn't intend to do 5
miles but there is a story....I wanted 2 miles to keep my streak alive. After
the first mile I felt good and decided to make it 3. At 1.5 miles mother
nature made my bowels start to rumble. I could tell time was of the essence!!
I was closer to the park port-a-potty than home so continue to it. That was
2.5 miles from home so shazzam...I had 5 miles and a safe visit to the port-a-potty!!
TMI

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1710120330>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1710120330</a>

lrb - Tuesday, May 2, 2017 at 13:39:30 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

About 7 at about 15. Mike, you're a riot. Tracy, you're a mazing.

tlz - Wednesday, May 3, 2017 at 01:08:16 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Mike, I would've opted for nature over the porta potty in favor of keeping
my run shorter. LOL  Anyway, you inspired me to get my tired, achy body back
out there today.  5 miles/10:10 pace.  Knee a tad wonky but should be fine.
Also got new shoes delivered today.  Will maybe try them out on Thurs.

MCT - Wednesday, May 3, 2017 at 10:37:38 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

7 miles in Tewksbury MA. Pace = 11:56. Nice morning.

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1708156422>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1708156422</a>

lrb - Thursday, May 4, 2017 at 09:20:25 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

did Scottish Rite sans Apple loop both yesterday and day before yesterday.
Very slow. 7+ miles each day.

ceb - Friday, May 5, 2017 at 18:27:32 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

I've been going through a tough period that best not be brought up
here.  It involved someone I used to work with.  But it's over.  I
ended it.  It was not easy - and took over a year to be resolved. 
Way too long I now see. All for the better I hope.

Congratulations to all of you on your accomplishments.
  
3 miles in the rain today.  Groton Farm loop once.  First run since
Sunday. Pace 9:18.  Have not felt at all like running -- until today.
Glad I did.

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1716161214>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1716161214</a>

tlz - Saturday, May 6, 2017 at 01:36:39 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

I've been delinquent.  I ran another 5 on Wed. - 9:50 pace.  On Thurs., I
walked 3+ around a 15 min. pace.  Will be doing a lot of walking at 3 Days
so wanted to remind myself what it would feel like.

RGT : Runner Group Therapy
Sorry to hear you're going through a rough spot, Chip.  Lately, I've tried
to reframe the difficult times as serving a purpose to make us more appreciative
of the conflict-free, happier times.  And I've been more forgiving of myself
when I don't feel like running. Sometimes you need the mental break and doing
nothing just feels good.  Hang in there.

lrb - Saturday, May 6, 2017 at 08:56:28 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Real short, slow 3+ on an abbreviated Newington 'Nihilator yesterday. 5k race
in Woodstock, CT this morning.

Can't top Tracy's comments on your recent decision to bring your situation
to a needed end. Well done Chip.

Best of luck to you Tracy on Friday the 19th.

lrb - Saturday, May 6, 2017 at 08:59:14 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

You forgot the

<img src=RGT.JPG>

Tray.

MCT - Saturday, May 6, 2017 at 13:22:40 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Went out while it was raining this morning and did 10 miles in Nassahegan
Forest and Sessions Woods. Foggy and misty. It was so peaceful. Great time
to clear one's head.  Did 8 yesterday and 7 on Thursday.

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1717440786>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1717440786</a>

lrb - Saturday, May 6, 2017 at 21:15:32 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Decent 5k in Wolcott, CT this morning. Rain fell at the end of the awards.
1st in my division (70+). 27:18 8:50 pace. Linda took pix.

<a href=https://www.facebook.com/media/set/?set=oa.1947622142135340&type=1>https://www.facebook.com/media/set/?set=oa.1947622142135340&type=1</a>

tlz - Sunday, May 7, 2017 at 11:55:29 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Ran 12 with Joe on Sat. - 10:15 pace.  We ran down the rail trail and at mile
9, stopped at the newly opened Witchcraft Brewery for a pint of beer and
then ran home.  There's also a second brewery on the rail trail less than
3 miles away from this one.  Witchcraft was hoppin' for a Saturday afternoon.
Get it? ;)

Lee, I messed up on the Runner Group Therapy and didn't copy the image text.

MCT - Sunday, May 7, 2017 at 14:57:48 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Ran twice today. Early morning 5 miles then the Ganem 5K(ish) race in Plymouth.
I think the distance was more like 2.9 miles. Finish time on the race was
25:14 at a 8:32 pace. Lee ran as well before heading off to the race in Wolcott.
54 miles for the week.

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1719932942>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1719932942</a>

lrb - Sunday, May 7, 2017 at 20:49:35 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

1st race: 5k Plymouth, CT (Terryville) (last mile was around Lake Winfield)

9:43 pace 28:29 2nd in division. Had to leave for Wolcott race so if I got
anything hopefully somebody picked it up.

<a href=https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1720715820>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1720715820</a>

<a href=http://greystoneracing.net/pages/Race%20Results%202017/Terryville%205.7.17.txt>http://greystoneracing.net/pages/Race%20Results%202017/Terryville%205.7.17.txt</a>

---------------------------------------------------

2nd race: 5k Wolcott,CT 1st in division 29:48 9:47 pace

<a href=https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1720706785>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1720706785</a>

-------------------------------------------------

3rd race: 6k trail race 50-99 division! Oxford, CT

<a href=https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1720711627>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1720711627</a>

<a href=http://fasttracktiming.com/race-result/run-the-rock-hike-the-hike-oxford-ct/#/results::1494187906746>http://fasttracktiming.com/race-result/run-the-rock-hike-the-hike-oxford-ct/#/results::1494187906746</a>

This last race was my 100th 169 town.

tlz - Sunday, May 7, 2017 at 22:04:10 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

5 miles/10:15 pace.  Ran with Joe down to Camp Sloper to say hi to the folks
doing the 600 minute ultra (10 hour).  Saw Emmy Stocker, Lou Loban, and Torpedo.
Runners' legs were covered in mud.  Apparently, the trail was a big mess
from the rain.

Lee and Mike, nice job on your races!  Lee, you're on fire with all of your
racing.  I'm confused though - you did a 5K in Wolcott on Sat. and Sun.?

MCT - Sunday, May 7, 2017 at 22:36:59 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Lee ... Plymouth gives awards to only first place finishers. I was 2nd in my
age group as well. But nice job getting in three races today.

lrb - Sunday, May 7, 2017 at 23:57:32 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

My bad. They begin w/ the same letter. Am I forgiven? My Saturday race was in
<b>Woodstock</b>. My today race was in <b>Wolcott</b>.

Tray, you are perceptive reader.

ceb - Tuesday, May 9, 2017 at 03:33:11 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Tracy (and Lee) thanks for your runner group therapy comments.  I
appreciate them! I've been letting myself take a break as you talked
about it Tracy.  Things are going better now.  Feeling better too.

Lee, nice work on all your races.  100 towns is quite an
accomplishment for sure!

And Mike, your Nassahegan Forest and Session
Woods run the other day sounded like a nice peaceful one.

3 miles today for me in Groton/Ayer.  Took it slow.  Good day.

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1722847265>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1722847265</a>

MCT - Tuesday, May 9, 2017 at 11:09:15 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

7 miles today and did 7 miles on Monday. 12+ minute pace. Good news is that
it's the time of year where the headlamp is off by 5:00am!

<img src=SAS.JPG>

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1723261149>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1723261149</a>

lrb - Tuesday, May 9, 2017 at 23:27:44 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

<a href=https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1724552598>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1724552598</a>

About 8 miles at about a 15 min. pace. Up the hill to Cedar Hill Cemetery,
counterclockwise around the cemetery and then back home. Beautiful place
