MCT - Wednesday, May 10, 2017 at 10:59:40 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

8 miles on the Vermont/New Hampshire line near Dartmouth. Pace = 12:17. 

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1725192229>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1725192229</a>

lrb - Thursday, May 11, 2017 at 20:03:28 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

On Wednesday I repeated what I did on Tuesday (about 8 up to the cemetery,
around, and back). Bought new Brooks Adrenaline GTS 17 shoes. Paid a lot of
money for them.

<img src=http://primepuzzle.com/tpf/brooks_adrenaline_GTS_17.png>

Am racing with Brent in Race in the Park on Saturday and running a 1 and a 3
mile in Suffield, CT at 9 and 9:30 on Sunday. This will be a bit of a celebration:
it is my 101st town.

ceb - Friday, May 12, 2017 at 19:21:52 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

18.59 miles last week

5 miles in 9:00/mile pace.  Into Ayer and back.  Grateful for the
nice weather today and for talking with and listening to a new friend named Jenny.  Good
luck with those new shoes Lee.  And have a good 101st!

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1729484121>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1729484121</a>

MCT - Saturday, May 13, 2017 at 13:13:28 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

15 miles of roads and trails. Tried a new section of the Tunxis trail on Johnnycake
Mountain. Then down to Sessions for more familiar trails. Beat the rain!!

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1730662914>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1730662914</a>

lrb - Saturday, May 13, 2017 at 16:54:34 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

<a href=https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1731050704>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1731050704</a>

28:05 9:04 pace at Race in the Park. Brent ran 21 flat.
Suffield 1 and 3 mile tomorrow morning. Will be wet. Amy C., her Dad Dan,
Debbie Solinsky and a few other friends were there.

MCT - Sunday, May 14, 2017 at 11:51:07 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

8 miles out to Sessions Woods. 12:48 pace. Actually a very nice morning for
a run. Did 60 miles this week. Congrats Lee on the races and towns.

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1732720478>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1732720478</a>

lrb - Sunday, May 14, 2017 at 17:31:08 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Ended up running all three races, 1 mile, 3 mile, 1 mile. Here's the 3 mile.

<a href=https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1733538877>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1733538877</a>

<img src=http://primepuzzle.com/tpf/101_r.jpg>

ceb - Sunday, May 14, 2017 at 23:58:47 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

6 miles at 9:44/mile.  Took the Groton Farm Loop twice. Misty light
rain.  280 ft elevation gain.

That was quite a day of running for you, Lee.  The pattern of your 3
miler was interesting with the track and all that out-and-back
looping. The Saturday 5k pace of 9:04 was decent, too.  Nice work!

20.09 miles for the week  

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1734113083>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1734113083</a>

MCT - Monday, May 15, 2017 at 10:32:48 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

8 miles at a 12:43 pace. Feels like October.

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1734610587>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1734610587</a>

tlz - Monday, May 15, 2017 at 12:22:21 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

I didn't log any of my runs last week:
Tues. 5 m/9:45
Wed. 6 m/9:30
Sun. 7 m/9:25
A big 18 miles for the week!  How's that for a taper? :P  T-5 days for the
48 hour.

Congrats to you, Lee, on your 101st town!  What's the occasion for the pretty
outfit? ;)

lrb - Monday, May 15, 2017 at 21:23:27 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

It's a tradition that you wear a tutu for your 100th town. I kinda went overboard
and ran 3 races instead of 2 last Sunday (making my 100th town an unplanned
one in Oxford). So ... we celebrated my 101st town in Suffield.

"Ran" 2+ at a ~16 today. Just didn't feel like doing more.

ceb - Monday, May 15, 2017 at 23:33:31 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

4 miles at 9:28 pace. Took it easy.  Wore my new shoes -- the ones
that gave me trouble in the later weeks of the Boston training.  Put
inserts in them.  There didn't seem to be any soreness today.  Some
remains though.  Tried keeping the pace down a bit today.  Cloudy. 
Looking forward to more sun.

Thanks Tracy for asking about Lee's dress.  I kinda wondered what was
going on there, but was too chicken to ask since I thought it could
have been a green under-jacket tied to his waste. Looked rather cool
actually -- like some kinda hulla thing.

Lee, 2 miles sounds good enough.  And recognizing it as being ok enuf
was even better!  Happy Belated 101st Town Day!

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1735802178>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1735802178</a>

ps.  Is it just me or do we not have Chariots of Fire anymore.  I love the spring
flowers but does this mean I can't have my cake and eat it too?

lrb - Tuesday, May 16, 2017 at 15:38:10 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Back by popular demand ... Chariots of Fire. Turn your volume up. Tell me
if it doesn't work.

<a href=https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1737496530>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1737496530</a>

Did 2+ @ ~ 15 min. pace on an abbreviated Newington 'Nihilator. How 'bout
this weather!

I'm running the Newington Library 5k on Sunday. Am actually considering running
the Newport Marathon in October ...

MCT - Wednesday, May 17, 2017 at 10:52:42 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

8.5 miles in Hyannis MA this morning. Pace was 11:19. Ran on two different
beaches at sunrise. Yesterday did 8 miles in White River Junction. Good luck
Tracy at 3 Days.

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1738409076>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1738409076</a>

tlz - Wednesday, May 17, 2017 at 21:23:11 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

<img src=NRRC.JPG>

No running this week and the nerves are starting to set in.  Joe left with
Sarah and Ian for NJ.  Their 72 hour race starts tomorrow at 9 am.  It's
going to be another hot day tomorrow so I am glad that I'm not starting!
I'll be driving down to NJ on Fri. morning for my 9 am start.  I think the
RD is posting updates on Facebook - there's a 3 Days page.  I'll text Lee
periodically as well.  Thanks for the well wishes!

lrb - Thursday, May 18, 2017 at 18:29:48 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Two very short runs, one this morning, one yesterday. Look forward to your
texts Tray. Thinking of Joe. Will be of you tomorrow.

MCT - Saturday, May 20, 2017 at 12:55:50 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Last night I did the Meridan Midnight run for Relay of Life. There was a
1 miler at 12:05 for the 169 group. My time was 8:10 which shows why I don't
try to compete in short races. The girl(was a teenager) who won finished
the mile in 6:10. Adam was 2nd with a 6:15 finish! Fast. I went to bed at
1:30 and went back out at 6:00am for 8 miles in Sessions Woods. Good luck
Tracy and Joe.

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1743863006>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1743863006</a>

tlz - Monday, May 22, 2017 at 00:02:43 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Quick race report. I had a blast this year at 3 Days, despite the ridiculous
heat on Fri.  Thursday was even worse for the first day of Joe, Sarah, and
Ian's race.  Results...

90 miles for me in the 48 hour race - way under what I wanted to do (127)
but I really had such a good time and figured that's actually a pretty damn
good effort, considering my training and the weather.  

For the 72 hour race:
Joe - 129 miles
Sarah - 81 miles
Ian - 86 miles

Miscellaneous tidbits:
Sarah and I both had blisters.  Ian and Joe - nothing!  So unfair!  

1st year of the 6 day race.  My 60 year old lawyer friend from Cheshire,
Fred, ran 365 miles over 6 days.  

Joe and I got our asses kicked by seniors!
In the 72 hour race, there was a 78 year old male who ran 132 miles!
In the 48 hour race, there was a 77 year old female who ran 105 miles!
I think they are both world records for their age group.  Holy freakin' crap!

ceb - Monday, May 22, 2017 at 01:29:24 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

This music is awesome!!!
Chip's been slackin' this week.  3.04 miles today at 10:04 / mile. 
Took the Groton Farm wildflower garden route.

Weekly Summary:  7.04 miles!  

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1747629986>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1747629986</a>

<img src= NRRC.JPG>

I might periodically post some of these cool wild flower images
as they flower.  First varieties are blooming now.  This one's a Lupin. 
(Lupinus polyphylus).  Image taken by Paul Slichter in 2007.

<img src = http://www.primepuzzle.com/charles/lupin.jpg>

Habitat:  Full sun to part shade.  
Horticultural Zone: 4-7
Height: about 18"
Bloom: Late May
Type: Perennial
Color(s): many varieties and colors
The ones on my run are violet.
Culure: Seed

MCT - Monday, May 22, 2017 at 10:36:52 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Congrats Tracy. Impressive numbers for all especially with the heat. Fred
is unbelievable because he does nearly 100 every week as normal runs!

Today I ran in Portsmouth NH. 8 miles at a 11:46 pace. One of my favorite
spots because I get to run out on the islands.I'm working in York ME at 8:00am
so had to come up on Sunday night. Yesterday I did 10 miles in Nassahegon
Forest.

