tlz - Monday, May 29, 2017 at 00:09:51 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Well, I went from 95 miles last week to 2 this week.  LOL  I hurt my ankle
during the first night of my 48 hour race.  The top of it - where the crease
is when you stand, walk, or run.  It flared up on and off in varying amounts
of intensity during the remainder of the race and has been hurting all week.
So I opted to give it a really good rest.  Walked 2 miles around the block
and it is still sore.  I'll be taking it easy this week and leaving for a
cruise to Bermuda on Sat.!  Lee, hope your knee is feeling better.  

ceb - Monday, May 29, 2017 at 01:52:33 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Another restful week for me.  Took a holiday from running and it
feels like it may have done some good.  Took it easy today on a 3
mile run at 9:47 / mile.  Total mileage for the week -- 6! -- which
is not to be confused with 720 miles ..... :)  because Professor Lee taught me that
6 factorial or 6! = 6x5x4x3x2x1 = 720 miles!

Going to try to be more serious this coming week.  Looking to do just 18.

