еееееее<head>

<title>"Brickyarders' Log"</title>

<script src=http://primepuzzle.com/runlog/kurt-grigg-september.js></script>

</head>

<body>

<table align=center width=89%><tr><td>

<pre><a href=http://primepuzzle.com/runlog/september_2016.htm><img title="Brickyarders' Log" src=http://primepuzzle.com/tpf/bricks.61.25.jpg></a><font size=+1><b>

tlz - Friday, September 2, 2016 at 00:44:40 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

7.5 miles - did 6 x 90 sec. hill repeats ranging from 7:28 to 8:02 pace, followed
by 4 miles at 8:43 pace.  I'm pooped!  My left Achilles is also killing me
so hope that doesn't become an issue. 

ceb - Friday, September 2, 2016 at 01:31:04 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

5.05 miles @ 9:42 pace

Tracy, that was one amazing workout!  You desearve a rest!

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1332691856>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1332691856</a>

lrb - Saturday, September 3, 2016 at 13:10:49 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)


<a href=https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1335456376>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1335456376</a>

Very circuitous route w/ the Glastonbury group this morning. About 8 miles
@ about 10:50 pace. Coolish!

I agree, that was one great workout Tray.

MCT - Saturday, September 3, 2016 at 13:56:16 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

12 miles at a 10:42 pace on the Larkin Bridal Path Trail. From Nauguatuck
to the Oxford Airport. Nice easy trail similar to Airline but a little more
rough and tight. Doing the Haddam Neck 5K on Sunday.

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1335553109>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1335553109</a>

tlz - Saturday, September 3, 2016 at 22:48:25 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Thanks Bradley bros.!  Ran 8.5 miles today with 7 miles at 8:35 pace.  Supposed
to do 16 tomorrow.  

ceb - Saturday, September 3, 2016 at 23:11:43 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

5.09 miles at a 10:01 pace Friday though Ayer center (flat)

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1336622993>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1336622993</a>

6.23 miles today at a 12:11 pace (with rest stops) with the Concord Runners.
Very hilly trail running.  356 foot elevation gain.

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1336623121>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1336623121</a>

MCT - Sunday, September 4, 2016 at 17:25:26 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Ran the Haddam Neck 5K this morning. Came in 3rd in my age group with a 27:43.
8:55 pace. Brian Walker beat me by about 10 secs. Course is flat except for
a steep but short hill at 2 miles. 59 miles for the week. Not doing New Haven
as I am running long locally on Monday.

<a href=https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1338580064>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1338580064</a>

tlz - Monday, September 5, 2016 at 01:13:14 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

Nice job on the 5K, Mike!

I went out at about 4:15 today.  It was so nice out - still a little hot
in the sun but in the shade, it was awesome.  I ran 16 miles total/9:25 pace.
 Starting at mile 10, I did 7 x 90 sec. surges @7:35 pace with 5 min. rest
in between.  Nice, strong run but definitely felt it by that 6th repeat!

43 miles for the week.

4 weeks until Apple Harvest and 8 weeks until the marathon.

ceb - Monday, September 5, 2016 at 02:28:36 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

4.58 miles / 10:22 pace

<a href = https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1339380177>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1339380177</a>

28.05 miles for the week.  On plan.

MCT - Monday, September 5, 2016 at 12:29:03 (GMT) (subtract 4 for local time)

12 miles in Burlington. 12:50 PACE. Felt like shit...ran like shit...looked
like shit!!! <img src=SAS.JPG>

<a href=https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1339954734>https://connect.garmin.com/modern/activity/1339954734</a>

