<img src=Nancy_Hilton_25.jpg>

Reading three books right now: East of Eden (2nd time thru, bugged me couldn't
remember most of it ... but do remember that it was a great work), Our Mathematical
Universe: My Quest for the Ultimate Nature of Reality (Max Tegmark), and
The Principles of Psychology by William James. Soooo glad I found you on
Facebook; I've wanted a way to correspond in addition to regular mail. Would
you on share with me a cell and or email address?

Tue 8:43pm

Sure! I was waiting and waiting to write to you until I had something to
truly write about. My email address is nancy.hilton.ct@gmail.com and my phone
number is 860-819-5493. I have heard that East of Eden is a truly masterful
novel! I took an online AP Psychology Course and learned a bit about William
James, though I confess it was not that much. The second book you mentioned
sounds weighty!!

Nancy! You've made my day!

I am currently reading Stuff Matters by Mark Miodownik which is about a select
few materials in our world and their amazing properties. It is very eye opening.
I am also reading the Tales of Sherlock Holmes, which I highly recommend.
The cases are fascinating. I also started a Brief History of Time by Stephen
Hawking and am working my way through that, although it is at a slower pace.
I fear that soon I may have to put these books aside as I become deluged
with my college studies, I leave tomorrow morning!! But while I am at college
I will be reading the Iliad by Homer, Euclid's Elements, Introduction to
Ancient Greek, and some short essays from ancient greeks about plant biology
and plant/animal comparison.

Oh Good! I am sorry it took me so long to get in touch, I was waiting until
I had a lot to say, I promise I wasn't ignoring you!

I clearly now have a new person to give me ideas. I never thought you were
ignoring me. Thank you so much for your contact info and for these three
long messages. I have one other friend who has been feeding me with book
suggestions and she is really good at it. I was amazed by your response to
the three I am reading now. It's a rare person that responds directly like
that. Either because they have some knowledge or recognize the potential
of something. William James is going to be tough going but I've plowed thru
quite a few in recent years and I ain't done yet. I promise I won't take
time away from your studies. I start my Tunxis tutoring in about a week.
Have a great first year at St John's College.

Thank you so much! I am very excited. My address is

Nancy Hilton
St. John's College
60 College Avenue Annapolis, MD 21401

Please write to me anytime!

I will!! Thank you. I was going to ask you for this too but then I figured
just using you name and looking up the college's address would probably work.
And now I know it will. Goodnight!

Goodnight!

