  Available Options (start with a  $  or  /  or  [  character):

  A - all user areas               D - all drives
  H - current area to highest      L - include $R/O files
  O - $SYS files only              Q - non $ARChived only
  R - reset disk system            S - include $SYS files
  T - order files by EXT type      V - show version
  1 - files with attrib 1          2 - files with attrib 2
  3 - files with attrib 3          4 - files with attrib 4

  Example - to purge all drv/users of .BAK, no verify:

                     B0>SD *.BAK $AND <ret>




